  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5430",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological activity against NCI-H2087 through multiple pathways, all involving the enzyme 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. This compound is a known target of Mollicellin N, and its interaction with NCI-H2087 is supported by three distinct but interconnected routes. Pathway 1 links Mollicellin N to NCI-H524, which in turn targets 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, ultimately leading to NCI-H2087. Pathway 2 provides a separate route, connecting Mollicellin N to A704, which also targets the same intermediate compound. Pathway 3 introduces a different target, P2X purinoceptor 1, which is inhibited by Mollicellin N and leads to NCI-H2087 via a distinct biochemical pathway. These findings suggest that Mollicellin N exerts its effects through multiple mechanisms, all of which converge on the 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid pathway. The evidence supports a complex, multi-targeted interaction, with the core mechanism involving the inhibition of a key metabolic or signaling compound. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mollicellin N to act as a broad-spectrum modulator of cellular processes, particularly in the context of NCI-H2087.",
